      "writtenOn": "2023-04-28T08:23:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hello,\n\nOur product need this patch to enable \"heap_flags\" for dma-buf heap drivers.\nAnd it was cherry-picked form KMI branch android13-5.15 which we worked with.\nBut now we are switching to KMI branch android14-5.15, which branch this patch was missing.\nWe need this patch.\nthanks.",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47403f1e_1de909f1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-28T08:35:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What out-of-tree heap dma code needs this?  Why not submit the needed changes upstream instead?",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c567f5f1_1561d50c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1973520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-28T09:54:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have a heap which need user-space send some configs in heap_flags to the dmabuf heap driver.\nWe can not upstream these \"heap_flags\", cause these heap_flags was hardware related in our SOC.\nOther vendor can\u0027t use it.\nIf we upstream this \"heap_flags\", other vendor will be confused.",
      "parentUuid": "47403f1e_1de909f1",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "907e0d4b_f2a0852a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1973520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-28T11:32:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do need this \"heap_flags\" hook now, from which we can enable \"heap_flags\".\nOur hardware related dmabuf heap need this heap_flags to bind with different hardware ID, as well as allocate buffer from differnt \"memory\".\nOther vendors can not get benefit from our \"heap_flags\", cause they can not recognize them.",
      "parentUuid": "c567f5f1_1561d50c",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "73552c22_b161a184",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1973520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T07:26:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "hello Greg,\n\n\"system\" and \"cma\" heap is the standard dmabuf heap.\nThe dmabuf heap flag limitation maybe used to format the interface for standard dmabuf heap like \"system\" and \"cma\" heap.\n\nBut vendor heaps are various, and it\u0027s hard to follow the \"standard heap flags\".\nExpcially for the situation, the heap flags designed accordding to the hareware.\nSo that, we need this vendor hook to deploy our dmabuf heap.\n\nThe other way comes to my mind, is seperate the \"dmabuf heap flags\", the lower 32bits is for standard heap flags, the upper 32bits is for vendor designed function.\nI can try to do that, but it could be a long discustion after that.\n\nThanks",
      "parentUuid": "907e0d4b_f2a0852a",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "439dcc2c_7821a33e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T23:44:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there was some history behind these dmabuf heap flags when John was upstreaming the heaps. Adding John and TJ to chime in.",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9783ebc_e8444bd6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1930620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T23:48:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is exactly the same as b/275191442#comment11",
      "parentUuid": "439dcc2c_7821a33e",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12616bb1_fefccada",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T23:51:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "dmabuf heaps intentionally avoid these sorts of opaque heap-specific flags.\n\nThe interface does have a (currently unused) flags field, but those are for well defined flags that are generic enough to appropriately apply to multiple heaps.\n\nI\u0027d recommend instead registering multiple heap types each with the specific property you\u0027d use the \"vendor designated flag\" for.\n\nAlternatively, you might try to abstract out and clearly express the flags need in a way that would be generally useful.",
      "parentUuid": "73552c22_b161a184",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "821da642_97738a1d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T23:53:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Worse case, if you really require special vendor-specific flags, consider creating a separate dmabuf exporter driver which would allow you to define your own vendor specific ioctl completely.",
      "parentUuid": "12616bb1_fefccada",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
