        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T18:40:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How did you resolve John\u0027s comments? The patch was abandoned to find a better design, what is that design?",
      "parentUuid": "8c0e07cf_8f408de1",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63d8387e_c52f67f6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1930620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T18:53:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the same cherry-pick as aosp/2507348 discussed at https://b.corp.google.com/issues/275191442#comment11. Without the hook, they need either a large number of heaps, or to abandon dma-buf heaps entirely and make their own exporter with support for their vendor specific flags. None of those solutions are ideal, and IMO this is the least-bad for their case.",
      "parentUuid": "5fc0c230_29a2f70f",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33ac589e_57fb0fc1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T20:03:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure extending upstream interfaces with vendor specific flags is least bad, as it makes for potential complications breaking vendor userland if future flags are added upstream.\n\nHaving a separate vendor specific exporter driver seems least likely to complicate things in my mind. I understand the frustration in having to create a similar but different interface, but out of tree vendor specific extensions of exiting upstream APIs is more problematic.\n\nI\u0027d strongly push folks to bring their requirements to the community, while also up-streaming drivers that use this extension so the upstream interface can grow in a way that satisfies the need.",
      "parentUuid": "63d8387e_c52f67f6",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "38df5133_a4bb86e7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1930620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T20:53:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I recognize those complications. I suggest we take this hook only up to 14-5.15 to allow them to rework their kernel and userspace for the next release, and reject any inclusion of this hook in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "33ac589e_57fb0fc1",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd72c7ae_a16103f3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-22T21:09:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If Zeku folks agree to that, I\u0027m ok with it. Though I want to impress strongly that this may cause complications to vendor userland in the future should any devices move forward to newer kernels via an uprev.",
      "parentUuid": "38df5133_a4bb86e7",
      "revId": "7caecbf68d44a672a03ff02d988236a30c8927d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
